---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import App from '../components/App.tsx';
import 'remixicon/fonts/remixicon.css';
import '../styles/index.css';
---

<Layout isApp={true} lang="en">
  <script is:inline src="/bezier.js" slot="head"></script>
  
  <App client:idle lang="en" slot="content" />

  <!-- Semantic HTML for Search Engine Crawlers & Screen Readers -->
  <section class="sr-only" aria-label="Tool Overview and Font Vectorization Guide">
    <h2>Google Font to SVG Path &amp; CAD DXF Converter</h2>
    <p>
      FontSVG is a free, 100% client-side tool to convert Google Fonts and custom fonts (.ttf, .otf, .woff, .woff2) into clean SVG paths (&lt;path d="..."&gt;) and CAD DXF drawings. In-browser parsing with OpenType.js and Maker.js.
    </p>
    <h3>Key Features</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>1,500+ Google Fonts</strong>: Instant client-side search and rendering.</li>
      <li><strong>Custom Font Upload</strong>: 100% private in-browser parsing for local TTF, OTF, and WOFF files.</li>
      <li><strong>Boolean Union (Weld)</strong>: Merges overlapping cursive and script glyph outlines into unified shapes for Cricut and laser cutting.</li>
      <li><strong>CAD DXF Export</strong>: Calibrated physical units (mm, cm, inch) for LightBurn, LaserCAD, and CNC routers.</li>
      <li><strong>Clean Vector Path</strong>: Instant one-click clipboard copying of raw &lt;path d&gt; strings for React and Three.js.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>How to Convert Fonts to SVG Path &amp; CAD DXF</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Select a Google Font or upload a local font file.</li>
      <li>Type your text and adjust font size, kerning, and line height.</li>
      <li>Check "Union" if converting cursive script fonts to weld overlapping outlines.</li>
      <li>Click "Copy SVG" for raw vector path data or click "SVG" / "DXF" to download.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Layout>
